A||||27||Lady Pegasus||What is with the youth of today? (ranting ensues)||||13||
Z||000000||Lady Pegasus||11-18-2001||12:10 AM||||Ok, ok...before I get a lot of slack, I know that I'm not that old...but still.  Went to see a movie today.  87 and I were having a good day.  Went to the club meeting, got some grub, laughed, all the good stuff.  So we go to see 13 Ghosts.  We get in the theatre, pick our seats and wait for the show to start.  Well, sitting in front of us were 3 kids who looked between 14-16 tops.  They were spaced out with one seat empty between each of them.  Another one comes to join them, and moves to the row behind (mine).  He proceeds to take up FOUR SEATS by laying down (side note....the armrests raised up, kinda like "love seats").  Well, no one could see him when he was laying down, so I can't even count how many people attempted to sit down.  He just proceeded to lay there, ignoring them.  Well, a couple comes up the isle and attempted to sit down.  There was an available seat on either side of 87 and I, so we just moved over one closer to said "kid."  I put my drink in the holder, which, opps, happened to be by his head.  I figured the schmuck had THREE OTHER SEATS to sprawl across, I needed to put my drink there.  I even said "Excuse me."  He sits up and begins muttering things under his breath.  I look at him and say, "Do you have a problem with me?"  He replys the question back at me with a few "colorful adjectives."  So of course, I let him know just what I think of him and his attitude and the whole "three seat" situation.  87 of course tries to cover my mouth, but frankly his hands aren't big enough.  : )  Anyhow.  Throughout the rest of the movie, he keeps muttering to his buddies and frankly I just kept boiling, keeping my mouth shut.  Then in comes the clincher.  A father and his 2 daughters come in.  There are two seats open on one side of him, and one seat open between he and I.  They ask if the seats are taken.  He says no.  The daughters sit down, and the father is standing there, waiting for the kid to move.  He doesn't.  The father then asks if he can move, he would like to sit next to his daughters.  The kid tells the father HE can move, because he likes his seat.  I finally got up and told the manager.  They came to the theatre, but when the kid saw the officer, he didn't move or do anything rude.  After they left, he quieted down, but every now and then he would get up and lean over to his buds in the row in front of him (still with a seat between each of them) to make remarks.  <BR>My point is, WHAT IS GOING ON HERE?!?!  I mean, sure, everyone knows the "unspoken rule" about usually one seat between each person/couple.  But this was just too much.  Maybe as I get older, I'm getting more cynical.  But to see, at least 15 people trying to sit in those four seats and for him to just ignore them.  It irks me.  Maybe I'm just anal retentive.<P>------------------<BR>Hey pretty....don't you wanna take a ride with me...through my world?||||reg||13
