Z||000009||Reality||11-18-2001||08:49 AM||||You know I'm 21 and I grew up with my parents trying to very hard to my brother and I the difference between right and wrong. And the whole time You can probably guess I was trying to fight them. Not because what they were teaching was wrong but because they were my parents. Well now being who I am, I just can't seem to find a way to thank them for being who they were and who they are. I love being who I am and I feel wouldn't be without them. And yes I was reprimanded on several occasions. I think that helped, I mean when mom said don't make me get your dad and his belt, I straightened up real good. And I also work in an environment where all day long I watch parents and their kids interact and my god what is wrong now-a-days. I've seen kids hit their parents, use foul language, cry until they go horse, and nothing is ever done! What I really love is when a parent goes into a store and tells their kids to go PLAY in a said part of the store and that they will be there in a couple of minutes. Isn't this being a little irresponsible? Okay that's my rant. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/realitysignature_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||11-18-2001||09:24 AM||||You know, I think pouring my Coke on the litte punks head would have been worth the $4 it cost.I have been known to hurl Mike & Ike's and Hot Tamale candy at repeat offenders in movie theaters.<P>I think even more distressing though, is parents who bring YOUNG kids to R rated movies. When I saw Three Kings in the theater there were several pre-teen kids, one as young as 5 or 6. Now, I don't cae that they are exposed to the graphic violence, but they tarnish my experience of said graphic violence with their constant yammering how they are <I>scared</I> and how <I>their psyches are being warped</I>. <BR>You know, if you're gonna breed, you better realize that dinner and a movie for the next 13 years is gonna have something to do with McDonalds and Disney.<P>AND ONE MORE THING THAT PISSES ME OFF!!!<BR>I can't stand it when someone has to come in to a movie theater bathed in stinky granny perfume! Makes me want to fart on them.||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroFanaticus2||11-18-2001||10:27 AM||||It's simple.<P>They have no respect.<BR>They have no true pride.<BR>They have worked for nothing.<BR>They think the world owes them a favor.<P>This is what happens when you remove morals and ethics from every public foundation.  And as decent people, we are forced to accept these little a$$holes who deserve to have their teeth kicked in.  And what's even worse, is that they are breeding at an alarming rate and we are also forced to pay for their illegitimate children that just grow up to vandalize and destroy the things we have worked for.  But, we are also made to believe that it is our fault for not giving these kids the positive opportunities that are needed at such a tender age.  I think a steel toe boot right up their ass would be a positive opportunity to start thinking about what they want in life.||||reg||1
