Z||000013||loafer87gt||11-18-2001||01:12 PM||||The way the system is set up right now the kids have more power than the parents. My Mom works at a highschool as a secretary and she used to love her job. That is until the strap and capital punishment were banned from the school. All the kids, myself included, behaved well and treated our teachers and principals with respect knowing that if we did something way our of line we would end up getting the strap. Now kids can tell the principal to F-off, hit the teachers, and they are basically left holding their dick and can't do a damn thing. They can suspend them for a couple of days, but this is probably what the kid wanted in the first place. Last year my Mom got in really hot water after the principal was having a really bad day at the school and told my mom to deal with a problematic kid who had just threatened one of the teachers during class. Instead of the usual suspension she made the kid do thirty pushup in the hallway during lunchhour so the other kids could see the kid doing them in the hall. Well, two days later she almost got fired because the kid was an indian and what she did was supposedly an act of racism. <P>With no body to discipline them, kids are going to keep getting worse and worse. A trend I seem to notice is that it's not the poor or single parent children who seem to be the most problematic, it's the kids with loaded parents who get everything handed to them that seem to have the least amount of respect for anyone. It's disgusting really.<p>[This message has been edited by loafer87gt (edited 11-18-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000014||LZeitgeist||11-18-2001||01:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>It's simple.<BR>They have no respect.<BR>They have no true pride.<BR>They have worked for nothing.<BR>They think the world owes them a favor.<P>This is what happens when you remove morals and ethics from every public foundation. And as decent people, we are forced to accept these little a$$holes who deserve to have their teeth kicked in. And what's even worse, is that they are breeding at an alarming rate and we are also forced to pay for their illegitimate children that just grow up to vandalize and destroy the things we have worked for. But, we are also made to believe that it is our fault for not giving these kids the positive opportunities that are needed at such a tender age. I think a steel toe boot right up their ass would be a positive opportunity to start thinking about what they want in life.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You've got <B>*my*</B> vote for President... <P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Cooter||11-18-2001||01:32 PM||||No respect. That is it, plain and simple and it comes from having no consequnces for their actions.<BR>At school last week, one of our new teachers was escourting 2 boys from the library because they could not behave. She told them that she was disappointed in them and turned to lead them away when one of the boys rolled his eyes at her and stuck out his tongue behind her back-with me watching! I asked him if he had a problem with his tongue and he just laughed and said to his buddy "Don't worry about them, they can't do anything to us." The boy's grandmother was there defending his actions within 20 minutes of the incident and was sure to tell the principal that no one would discipline their angel except for them. I can't wait until they get to the high school next year and try that crap with their principal.||||reg||1
